                <pb facs="0797" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">311.6124/56a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Commissioner at Riga</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Young</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-26T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26, 1920—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department of Labor desires to ship more deportees to Russia and inquires
                    possibility of landing vessel at Reval. Make no inquiries of Esthonians but
                    telegraph whether such deportees could proceed freely and safely into Soviet
                    Russia without previous arrangement with the Soviet authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
